  "notes": "Greyhollow, prototype design 11 §2 and §8.3, reworked 2026-10-14 to be believable: the castle sits in a hollow ringed by cliffs; the west, north and east roads enter through three passes the walls seal. Both gold mines lie outside the rim. A river runs down the east side, crossed by one bridge; a lake lies south-west. Cliffs and water block walking for everyone on the ground. Wall slots double as lane waypoints; the o_* nodes outside the rim only help bodies find their way round it. Tuned after the first playtest (2026-10-13): more gold (start 75, castle 25 a dawn) and 30% more enemies per group. Night 6: the warlord replaces the west brutes. Stage A2: raiders and skirmishers on nights 4-6 +15%, night 6 +15% more. The cliffs make walls seal their pass, so nights 5-6 raiders and skirmishers +10% (balanced bot back near 90%). Two archery range slots, one behind each side gate (11 §12.2).",
